    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b109f24c-5a3f-5a1b-a4e4-923c997546a8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Egremont Castle, Egremont, Cumbria, Whitehaven, River Ehen, Sussex, Yorkshire\n- People: George Wyndham, 3rd Earl of Egremont, Josceline Percy, Elizabeth Percy, Charles Seymour, Algernon Seymour, Sir Charles Wyndham, Baron Leconfield\n- Organizations/Roles: Borough of Copeland, Earl of Egremont, Duke of Somerset, Earl of Northumberland\n\nFacts:\n- Egremont is a market town, civil parish, and two electoral wards called North and South in the Borough of Copeland in Cumbria, England.\n- Egremont lies 5 miles south of Whitehaven and on the River Ehen.\n- Egremont Castle is located in the town of Egremont, Cumbria.\n- Josceline Percy, 11th Earl of Northumberland, formerly held lands including Egremont Castle, Cockermouth Castle, and Leconfield Castle.\n- Elizabeth Percy married Charles Seymour, 6th Duke of Somerset, and he inherited the Percy lands through that marriage.\n- Algernon Seymour, 7th Duke of Somerset and 1st Earl of Egremont, was the son of Charles Seymour and Elizabeth Percy.\n- Sir Charles Wyndham, 4th Baronet, inherited as one of Algernon Seymour's co-heirs and also inherited the Earldom of Egremont by special remainder.\n- Baron Leconfield was the eldest illegitimate son and adopted heir of George Wyndham, 3rd Earl of Egremont.\n- Baron Leconfield inherited Petworth House in Sussex, Egremont Castle and Cockermouth Castle in Cumbria, and Leconfield Castle in Yorkshire from George Wyndham, 3rd Earl of Egremont.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
